Interpretation: the local curvature is NOT constant across the whole range of
m -- it starts near c(gamma)/2 = (1-gamma)/gamma for m=O(1) and drifts toward
A(gamma) = (2-gamma)/(2 gamma) as m grows into the Theta(sqrt n) mesoscale that
dominates the outer sum S_n'. Both endpoints are individually consistent with
independently-verified facts (predecessor's c(gamma) at one end, this front's
T_prof at the other) -- the crossover itself, and the fact that it is A(gamma),
not c(gamma)/2, that governs the mass-dominant range, is this front's own,
newly disclosed, structural finding.
